  "description": "NaSbO₃ crystallizes in the cubic Fd̅3m space group. Na is bonded in a hexagonal planar geometry to six equivalent O atoms. All Na-O bond lengths are 2.56 Å. Sb is bonded to six equivalent O atoms to form corner-sharing SbO₆ octahedra. The corner-sharing octahedral tilt angles are 48°. All Sb-O bond lengths are 2.01 Å. O is bonded to two equivalent Na and two equivalent Sb atoms to form a mixture of distorted corner and edge-sharing ONa₂Sb₂ tetrahedra.",
